# Recall MCP daemon — X230 (systemd user unit)
# The Recall MCP daemon serves the fleet's semantic-recall queries over HTTP (FastMCP streamable transport) on port 3004, from the X230 where the SQLite databases live on local disk.  Phase 7 of the Recall project (approved 2026-07-28): the databases are WAL-mode, which is unsafe to touch over NFS — the store refuses it — so every remote machine queries this daemon over the tailnet instead of opening the files.  Embedding of query text is NOT done here: the daemon's client side resolves an embed node from =ROOTS/inference/nodes.toml= (honey, then the T480s) — the X230 runs no inference, by standing ruling.

# The unit binds =0.0.0.0= so both the tailnet and LAN faces answer; Tailscale ACLs govern who reaches it.  The throttle drop-in follows the X230 thermal policy from the Borg units above, tuned for an interactive service: idle-class scheduling would starve query latency, so this uses a niced two-core cap instead.


# [[file:../../../../services.org::*Recall MCP daemon — X230 (systemd user unit)][Recall MCP daemon — X230 (systemd user unit):1]]
[Unit]
Description=Recall MCP daemon (fleet semantic recall over HTTP)
Documentation=file:%h/HelmCortex/FORGE/scripts/recall/README.md
ConditionPathExists=%h/HelmCortex/FORGE/bin/recall

[Service]
Type=simple
Environment=PATH=%h/.guix-extra-profiles/core/core/bin:%h/.local/bin:/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
ExecStart=%h/HelmCortex/FORGE/bin/recall mcp --transport http --host 0.0.0.0 --port 3004
Restart=on-failure
RestartSec=30
KillMode=process

[Install]
WantedBy=default.target
# Recall MCP daemon — X230 (systemd user unit):1 ends here
